This VERSION file is the authoritative build identifier.
All visible labels, launcher, and window titles must match this version.

v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application, replacing a five-file
browser prototype that was reviewed and found not releasable.

v2.1.0 added a Tie bet alongside Banker or Player, moved the disclaimer to the foot of the window and
removed page scrolling. v2.2.x put the panels beside the betting column for half-screen use, gave the
bead plate a fixed 10 x 10 box of small colour-only hands and renamed the panels. v2.3.0 made PASS
record the table's result. v2.4.0 gave the Tie insurance its own stake.

v2.5.0 added the OCR spot-check tool, an accuracy readout built from the audit log, a working Gemini
model id (gemini-3.8-flash) and removed a phantom "stop" event from that log. v2.5.1 proved the
reading prompt against nine synthetic result displays (all nine correct, including 11px text, a
Chinese label and a busy table with decoy markers), made that check re-runnable with grading, and
fixed a crash when the model's quoted evidence contained non-Latin characters. v2.5.2 adds a
"Save a screenshot sample" button so a capture region can be judged without using a terminal.

IMPORTANT: the screen reader has never read the user's casino display and no calibration region has
been measured. Do not treat OCR as working until a real screenshot of the table reads correctly.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
